# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers straight off a bind mount, so they
# have to keep LF endings even when the repository is checked out on Windows
# with core.autocrlf=true -- /bin/sh reads a CRLF script as commands that end in
# a stray \r and fails with "not found" on the first line.
*.sh text eol=lf

# nginx reads these inside the container. Same reason as above: a CRLF that
# arrived from a Windows checkout ends up inside directive values, and the
# failure ("unknown directive") points at the wrong thing entirely.
*.conf text eol=lf
